    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0217" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690B.9321/1–854: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 143<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in the Republic of
                            China</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d143-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-12T21:09:00-05:00">January 12, 1954—9:09
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>647. Rangoon’s 665 rptd Taipei 128, Bangkok 148.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f2"/>
                    Assume Embassies Taipei and Bangkok conveyed text Burmese memorandum quoted
                        reftel to Chinese and Thai Governments.
                    Consider memorandum satisfactory basis for Joint Committee proceeding with
                    measures for further evacuation.</p>
                <p>Believe Committee should consider all outstanding questions and action at
                    diplomatic level should be required only on matters where Committee unable reach
                    agreement or act without decision governments concerned.</p>
                <p>Hope Chinese and Thai Governments concur this concept Committee’s role and
                    authorize Embassies their discretion discuss matter with Chinese and Thai
                    Governments assure representatives on Committee appropriately instructed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d143-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d143-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to Bangkok; repeated to Rangoon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d143-f2" n="2" xml:id="d143-f2-content">
                <p>Dated Jan. 8; it transmitted the text of a memorandum received that day from the
                    Burmese Foreign Office confirming Acly’s Jan. 3 conversation with Tun Shein.
                    (690B.9321/1–854)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
